  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it or `vite build`, because there is no shell or browser here. The physics behaviour (whether the chain actually propagates) is untested.\n\n- **Scene:** a wood table sits on a dark floor, with 30 tiles (0.2 × 1.0 × 0.5) along a gentle S-curve and a hue-cycled colour per tile. A ramp with two support pillars is at the start. A red metal ball rests near the top of the ramp. The scene has a hemisphere light, a neutral environment, and a shadow-casting directional light. The camera is computed from the layout bounds so the whole path fits in the 640×360 canvas.\n- **Physics:** a Rapier world from `physics.worldAsync`, stepped at a fixed 1/120 s with an accumulator in `app.onFrame` (capped at 16 steps per frame). Sleeping is off. Release is applied on a step boundary. Before release the ball is held in place on the ramp each step.\n- **Rendering:** each frame the body poses are written to the node handles, with quaternions converted to ZYX Euler angles to match the renderer.\n- **Buttons:** DOM `Release` and `Reset` buttons are overlaid at the bottom-left of the canvas. `Reset` calls `world.reset()` and falls back to manually restoring poses if that throws.\n- **Task state:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a frozen object republished every frame. A tile counts as toppled when its up axis is tilted more than 60° from vertical. The phase becomes `settled` after everything has been calm for 0.75 s, or after a 45 s simulated timeout.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set once the app is ready.\n\nThe main uncertainty is the ball's hit on the first tile. I raised the ramp end so the ball strikes the tile above its centre of mass, which should topple it forward rather than slide it. If the chain stalls, adjust the tile spacing, tile mass, or ramp height at the top of `src/main.ts`.\n\n",
